      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fiji focus",
          "heading": "James Ryan insists Ireland are not thinking about South Africa yet",
          "body": "James Ryan, who returns to the starting XV at lock alongside Tadhg Beirne, has played down talk of next Saturday's clash with the world champions. Speaking to RTÉ Sport, he said: \"We're not thinking about South Africa,\" adding, \"I know that's the boring answer, but it is the answer.\" Last year's 24-13 Dublin defeat to the Springboks, in which Ryan received a 20-minute red card, gives the fixture extra edge. He also wants Ireland to build on the 42-12 win over Argentina."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks name Beauden Barrett captain, Scott Barrett passed over",
          "body": "England restore Max Ojomoh at No 12, Fin Smith left out. Wallabies restore Carter Gordon at fly-half over Declan Meredith. Scotland's Darcy Graham returns on wing, Blair Kinghorn to full-back."
