      "edition": "Saturday 14 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching scrutiny",
          "heading": "Felipe Contepomi, under fire over results, says doing things well brings wins",
          "body": "Argentina head coach Felipe Contepomi faces a fierce wave of criticism over results, including a win over Wales bracketed by heavy home defeats to Scotland and England. Ahead of Italy, he says he wants the win first, but that the route to it is doing things well in the week. Winning is the goal, he said, yet the team can only control its own preparation. Argentina's last outing was a 42-12 defeat to Ireland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks name Beauden Barrett captain, Scott Barrett passed over",
